%I A401551 #19 Nov 09 2026 10:34:29
%S A401551 1,1,1,2,5,7,14,23,45,79
%N A401551 Number of combinatorial types of triangulations of the sphere with n vertices for which the volume of polyhedra of that type inscribed in the unit sphere has a local maximum at a strictly convex configuration.
%C A401551 a(14) >= 158.
%C A401551 The terms are derived numerically: random search with local optimization for each type. A type is counted if at least one inner local maximum is found. If multiple local maxima should exist for a type, the type is still only counted once. Apart from the mirror image of a chiral optimum, which belongs to the same plantri type, no type with more than one local maximum is known for n <= 13. Since a proof for the optimality of even the best configuration for n = 10, 11 and n >= 13 is not yet known, the remaining terms must be considered unproven despite massive numerical evidence.
%C A401551 Of the A000109(n) possible triangulations, A007037(n) result in no inscribable configurations. These yield 0 hits in the generation of point distributions, regardless of the number of random draws. See the linked files with the results from n = 6 to 12.
%C A401551 For n <= 13, each of the A401550(n) inscribable types was investigated, either via random configurations or via the construction of an ideal polyhedron using Rivin's method (see Hodgson, Rivin, Smith link).
%H A401551 The Combinatorial Object Server, <a href="https://combos.org/plantri">Generate plane triangulations and quadrangulations</a>, website interface to the program plantri.
%H A401551 Craig D. Hodgson, Igor Rivin, and Warren D. Smith, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/math/9210218">A characterization of convex hyperbolic polyhedra and of convex polyhedra inscribed in the sphere</a>, arXiv:math/9210218 [math.MG], 1992.
%H A401551 Hugo Pfoertner, <a href="/A401551/a401551_1.txt">List of numerically achievable maximum volumes for the possible triangulations of 6, 7, and 8 vertices</a>.
%H A401551 Hugo Pfoertner, <a href="/A339261/a339261.txt">List of numerically achievable maximum volumes for the 50 possible triangulations of 9 vertices</a>, 2026.
%H A401551 Hugo Pfoertner, <a href="/A339262/a339262.txt">List of numerically achievable maximum volumes for the 233 possible triangulations of 10 vertices</a>, Oct 29 2026.
%H A401551 Hugo Pfoertner, <a href="/A339263/a339263_1.txt">List of numerically achievable maximum volumes for the 1249 possible triangulations of 11 vertices</a>, Nov 03 2026.
%H A401551 Hugo Pfoertner, <a href="/A339259/a339259.txt">List of numerically achievable maximum volumes for the possible 7595 triangulations of 12 vertices</a>, Nov 02 2026.
%H A401551 Hugo Pfoertner, <a href="/A401551/a401551_2.txt">List of combinatorial types of triangulations of 13 vertices corresponding to the 79 convex local inner maxima</a>, Nov 07 2026.
%e A401551 a(12) = 45: among the A000109(12)=7595 triangulations, besides the icosahedron as the proven global maximum with volume A339259, there are 44 more where the condition of a local volume maximum can be achieved without a triangle of the polyhedron's surface degenerating in such a way that it becomes co-planar with a neighboring triangle. See the linked file for the results of a corresponding search.
%Y A401551 Cf. A000109, A007037, A081314, A339259-A339263, A401263, A401264, A401550.
%K A401551 nonn,hard,more,new
